<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">01072026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Thirty thousand displaced Palestinians have been barred from returning to Jenin refugee camp, where Israel is now building a permanent military base.</s> <s>Israeli forces occupied Jenin and Tulkarm in January of last year, bulldozing Area A — the zone the Oslo Accords assigned to Palestinian administration.</s> <s>Whether these families ever see their homes again may now depend on facts set in concrete.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Ukraine has formally ordered sixteen Gripen E fighters from Sweden, a contract valued near two and a half billion dollars.</s> <s>Built to fly from short roads and improvised runways, the jet lets squadrons scatter and survive under sustained missile threat — precisely the war Kyiv is fighting.</s> <s>European states are now committing frontline platforms, not just munitions, and that shift changes the war's arithmetic.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Kazakhstan has put the former editor-in-chief of the independent outlet Orda.kz on trial after months under house arrest.</s> <s>Gulnara Bazhkenova's prosecution tests how far a Central Asian state will reach to silence a critical newsroom, in a region where independent journalism survives on narrow ground.</s> <s>What the specific charges establish could set the precedent for every outlet that outlives the pressure to close.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Iran's six billion dollars in frozen assets remain untransferred, and that single financial clause now holds up a fragile ceasefire.</s> <s>Kushner and Witkoff have landed in Doha, but Qatar says no meeting with Iranian officials is even scheduled, and Tehran insists there's no direct channel.</s> <s>Article eleven governs whether the money is released at once or in tranches, and the deal's survival may hinge on it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A quarter of a million newborns each year stood to lose American citizenship until the Supreme Court blocked Donald Trump's order to end birthright citizenship by decree.</s> <s>The Fourteenth Amendment bars narrowing that right by executive fiat, a six-to-three majority held, with two of Trump's own appointees joining.</s> <s>Trump has called on Congress to legislate the change, moving the fight from the courts to the Capitol.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>El Salvador has packed nine hundred defendants into a single mass trial, with prosecutors demanding twenty thousand years for one alleged gang leader.</s> <s>A law passed under President Bukele now allows nine hundred suspects per proceeding, a shortcut to process the eighty thousand people swept up in his twenty twenty-two crackdown.</s> <s>Whether those sentences survive appeal, and how many cases ever reach a verdict, remains unknown.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Cuba's infant mortality rate has doubled, the United Nations reports, as forty-hour blackouts cut power to hospitals and break the cold chains that keep medicine viable.</s> <s>Washington effectively severed the island's oil supply in January through tariff threats, and the collapse has now reached the maternity ward.</s> <s>Havana calls the talks a wall, and has summoned July mobilizations as the crisis deepens.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Egypt has doubled the prices in its Beit al-Watan scheme, which sells dollar-priced land to citizens living abroad.</s> <s>The programme has netted more than seven billion dollars since twenty twelve, and brokers now resell half the plots into a speculative market the state itself is fuelling.</s> <s>A cash-strapped government is monetising land and access to plug a foreign-currency crisis, and the middlemen are pocketing the difference.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Britain has committed fifteen billion pounds to new defence spending, betting that mass-produced drones can offset the conventional forces it can no longer afford.</s> <s>London targets two point seven percent of national output by twenty twenty-nine, still below most European peers.</s> <s>The drone-maker TEKEVER has pledged four hundred million pounds toward British production, a wager that cheap machines can substitute for expensive platforms.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India has cut the price of a commercial cooking-gas cylinder by roughly one hundred eighty-four rupees, the first reduction since tensions in Western Asia squeezed supply.</s> <s>The relief traces directly to easing pressure on the Strait of Hormuz and a US-Iran ceasefire, showing how a distant waterway reaches the margins of a street vendor's stall.</s> <s>Further cuts depend on whether that calm holds across the region.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Nobel laureate Giorgio Parisi and Francesco Zamponi, working in Rome, say an artificial-intelligence model helped prove a jamming-physics relation that had resisted researchers for more than a decade.</s> <s>Published in a peer-reviewed journal, the work isn't a machine replacing mathematicians — it's a language model contributing a step inside a formal proof.</s> <s>Neither physicist has specified which step, leaving open just how far such reasoning can go.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>No approved therapy exists for the Ebola strain behind the Democratic Republic of Congo's current outbreak.</s> <s>Existing treatments target only the Zaire species, leaving Bundibugyo — the strain now spreading — with no authorized drug at all.</s> <s>Jean-Jacques Muyembe, the country's leading Ebola scientist, says a monoclonal antibody is in the works, and that the science is being driven from Kinshasa, not the West.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Pakistan, where summer temperatures routinely pass forty degrees Celsius, researchers are testing whether reflective paint and better airflow can cool homes without air conditioning.</s> <s>Aga Khan University's Jai Das is aiming at the poorest households, for whom even a switched-on cooler is a luxury the grid can't guarantee anyway.</s> <s>As glacial floods, drought and extreme heat converge, low-cost adaptation may be less a choice than a necessity.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>One hundred four governments pledged six point four billion dollars for marine protection at a summit in Mombasa, the first such conference hosted in Africa.</s> <s>Even as they pledged, delegates openly conceded that delivery on past ocean commitments has lagged badly.</s> <s>David Obura warned that nearly half of all coral species now face extinction, and nothing binds donors to the promises they make.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>China plans to spend two hundred ninety-five billion dollars building artificial-intelligence data centres, and the plan deliberately shuts foreign firms out.</s> <s>State-scale capital is being channelled to domestic chipmakers and cloud providers to bootstrap a self-sufficient AI stack behind a wall against American suppliers.</s> <s>The move accelerates a split of the global tech economy into two spheres that no longer interoperate.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Maldives has no home-grown answer to Temu, the Chinese platform now dominating conversation among local merchants who can't match its direct-to-consumer prices.</s> <s>Scattered across some twelve hundred islands, the country once relied on geography to protect its retail, and that same geography now leaves it exposed.</s> <s>As shipping reaches every atoll, the shopkeepers of Male are discovering how quickly a distant warehouse can hollow out a local economy.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>